IMPORT prelude

-- Civil Liability Act 2003 (Queensland) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library.
-- The Act's own days used here: 2 December 2002 and 1 December 2002 (ss 4(2), 61, 62), 1 July 2010 (s 85). The
-- Civil Liability Indexation Notice 2026 fixes amounts for "the 2026-2027 financial year" (1 July 2026 to 30 June
-- 2027). Notices for other financial years are not deposited.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Civil Liability Act 2003`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar day` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days from` `the start` `until` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the date` `the first` `falls before` `the second` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the first` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second`

GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the date` `the first` `falls on or after` `the second` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the first` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `the second`

-- The day a number of days after a day.
GIVEN `the days` IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `the days` `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS `the days`)

-- A financial year runs from 1 July to 30 June; it is named here by the calendar year in which it starts
-- (the 2026-2027 financial year is 2026).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the financial year starting in the year of` `the day` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the day` AT LEAST 7
    THEN DATE_YEAR `the day`
    ELSE DATE_YEAR `the day` MINUS 1

-- The one financial year for which an indexation notice is deposited (Civil Liability Indexation Notice 2026, ss 3-5).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day falls in the 2026-2027 financial year` `the day` IF
    `the financial year starting in the year of` `the day` EQUALS 2026
